  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Speculation regarding the status of Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka has emerged following reports suggesting he may have submitted a formal resignation letter to President Prabowo Subianto. These rumors have prompted inquiries among various political factions and legislative bodies. However, key parliamentary leaders, including representatives from the House of Representatives (DPR) and the People's Consultative Assembly (MPR), have explicitly stated that they possess no information or evidence regarding any such resignation. Meanwhile, the political opposition, specifically the Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle (PDIP), has questioned the validity of the reports, describing the situation as a potential political maneuver. In response to the uncertainty, government economic representatives, including the CEO of the Danantara Investment Management Agency, have sought to assure the public that the nation's economic foundations and the operations of state-owned enterprises remain unaffected by these reports.",
